{
  "version": "aed1dc225396f51e",
  "duration": 49.75,
  "voice": "af_sky",
  "audioSha256": "d9e03ec3df23393155e56bb10b4c856300c8b2d12a1705c9e7949ed079c40557",
  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 5.04,
      "paragraph": 0,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 458,
          "end": 543
        }
      ],
      "text": "Alan Dershowitz sued respondent, a major news network, alleging that it defamed him."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.04,
      "end": 14.08,
      "paragraph": 0,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 545,
          "end": 725
        }
      ],
      "text": "Because Dershowitz is a “public person,” our precedents required him to prove not only the elements of common-law defamation, but also that the network acted with “actual malice.”"
    },
    {
      "start": 14.08,
      "end": 21.04,
      "paragraph": 0,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 798,
          "end": 955
        }
      ],
      "text": "Predictably, Dershowitz did not prevail under that exacting standard, which this Court created in New York Times Co. v. Sullivan."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.04,
      "end": 26.0,
      "paragraph": 0,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 957,
          "end": 1033
        }
      ],
      "text": "Dershowitz now asks this Court to overrule Sullivan and related precedents."
    },
    {
      "start": 26.0,
      "end": 33.8,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 1034,
          "end": 1161
        }
      ],
      "text": "The “actual malice” standard for public figures “bears ‘no relation to the text, history, or structure of the Constitution.’”"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.8,
      "end": 41.32,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 1556,
          "end": 1693
        }
      ],
      "text": "Instead, the founding generation believed that, if anything, public figures had stronger claims for damages when they were defamed."
    },
    {
      "start": 41.32,
      "end": 46.36,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 0,
          "start": 1794,
          "end": 1867
        },
        {
          "page": 1,
          "start": 78,
          "end": 106
        }
      ],
      "text": "I and others have thus called for reconsideration of the actual-malice standard for public figures."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.36,
      "end": 49.4,
      "paragraph": 1,
      "ranges": [
        {
          "page": 1,
          "start": 323,
          "end": 378
        }
      ],
      "text": "I would have granted certiorari to do so in this case."
    }
  ],
